  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Aecom Technical Services obligated $225M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date across 443 awards, with an average award size of $509K. Obligations fell 39.5% year over year. Year-by-year obligations show a peak at $719M in FY24 and a decline to $373M in FY25 before reaching $225M in FY26. The Department of Defense is the top buyer with $103M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $67.9M and the General Services Administration with $26.3M. Engineering Services is the largest market by obligation at $191M, far ahead of other NAICS categories such as Architectural Services at $20.1M and Remediation Services at $6.1M. Several markets show minimal or zero obligations in FY2026 to date, including Facilities Support Services and Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities. The dataset covers contract obligations except where tables list total contract values for largest awards and expiring contracts. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Aecom Technical Services primary federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest customer with $103M in obligations. The Department of Homeland Security follows with $67.9M and the General Services Administration with $26.3M. Other buyers include the Department of Transportation at $11.2M and NASA at $4.9M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets account for most federal spending with Aecom Technical Services?",
        "body": "Engineering Services accounts for the bulk of obligations at $191M. Architectural Services is the second-largest market at $20.1M, and Remediation Services is next at $6.1M. Several markets show very small or zero obligations in FY2026 to date, such as Facilities Support Services at $0."
      }
    ]
